     _f_r_i_e_n_d_s is specified in the netgroup file with users mapped to their re‐
     mote credentials and root mapped to UID 0 and GID 10.  It is exported
     read-write and the hosts in “friends” can mount either _/_u_s_r or
     _/_u_s_r_/_l_o_c_a_l.  It is exported to _1_3_1_._1_0_4_._4_8_._1_6 and _g_r_u_m_p_y_._c_i_s_._u_o_g_u_e_l_p_h_._c_a
     with users mapped to their remote credentials and root mapped to the user
     and groups associated with “daemon”; it is exported to the rest of the
     world as read-only with all users mapped to the user and groups associ‐
     ated with “nobody”.

     _/_u is exported to all hosts on the subnetwork _1_3_1_._1_0_4_._4_8 with root mapped
