BBUUGGSS
     The export options are tied to the local mount points in the kernel and
     must be non-contradictory for any exported subdirectory of the local
     server mount point.  It is recommended that all exported directories
     within the same server filesystem be specified on adjacent lines going
     down the tree.  You cannot specify a hostname that is also the name of a
     netgroup.  Specifying the full domain specification for a hostname can
     normally circumvent the problem.

     Regarding --aallllddiirrss, because NFS mount filehandles are filesystem wide the
     --aallllddiirrss option applies to exports of the entire filesystem — even mount
     points that are higher up elsewhere in the directory hierarchy.  Hence if
     the server has a filesystem _/_e_x_p_o_r_t and you wished to export the sub-di‐
     rectory

           /export/root/client -alldirs client.foo.com

     you must realize that this also allows mounts to be requested against
     other locations in the _/_e_x_p_o_r_t filesystem; thus the host client.foo.com
     is also permitted to mount the directory _/_e_x_p_o_r_t_/_r_o_o_t_/_c_l_i_e_n_t_2 if it ex‐
     ists.

